# Letting the Browser Decide

- `width: auto;` (default for block elements) – fills the available space.
- `height: auto;` – grows with content.

If content is larger than a fixed height/width, it overflows. Use `overflow` to control this:
```css
.box {
  width: 200px;
  height: 100px;
  overflow: hidden;  /* clip content */
  /* or overflow: auto; for scrollbars when needed */
}
```
`overflow-x` and `overflow-y` allow separate control.
